steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∉ {\"approve_payout\"} THEN policy returns (True, \"Tool '<tool_name>' is not critical and is always allowed.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"approve_payout\" AND any of {case_id, amount, status, coverage_limit, authenticity, is_preexisting, exclusion_applies, suggested_payout, claim_amount, deductible_applied} is missing THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing required data for approve_payout: <list_of_missing>\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"approve_payout\" AND status ≠ \"Active\" THEN policy returns (False, \"Policy status is '<status>' (required: Active).\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"approve_payout\" AND authenticity ≠ \"High\" THEN policy returns (False, \"Document authenticity is '<authenticity>' (required: High).\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"approve_payout\" AND is_preexisting = true AND exclusion_applies = true THEN policy returns (False, \"Claim involves a pre‑existing condition with exclusion; must deny.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"approve_payout\" AND amount > coverage_limit THEN policy returns (False, \"Requested amount <amount> exceeds coverage limit <coverage_limit>.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"approve_payout\" AND amount > suggested_payout THEN policy returns (False, \"Requested amount <amount> exceeds suggested payout <suggested_payout>.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"approve_payout\" AND amount > (claim_amount - deductible_applied) THEN policy returns (False, \"Requested amount <amount> exceeds claim amount after deductible (<max_allowed>).\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"approve_payout\" AND all of the following hold: status = \"Active\", authenticity = \"High\", NOT(is_preexisting = true AND exclusion_applies = true), amount ≤ coverage_limit, amount ≤ suggested_payout, amount ≤ (claim_amount - deductible_applied) THEN policy returns (True, \"approve_payout allowed: all prerequisite checks satisfied.\")"
  }
]

These IF‑THEN rules capture every precondition the policy enforces before the critical **approve_payout** tool may be executed, as well as the default allowance for all other (safe) tools. They also describe the exact post‑condition messages the policy returns for both allowed and denied cases, ensuring the agent can reason about compliance with the security request.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ∉ WHITELISTED_TOOLS THEN reject WITH reason \"Tool not permitted\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ≠ \"approve_payout\" THEN accept (no further checks)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = \"approve_payout\" AND any of {\"case_id\",\"amount\",\"status\",\"coverage_limit\",\"authenticity\",\"is_preexisting\",\"exclusion_applies\",\"suggested_payout\",\"claim_amount\",\"deductible_applied\"} is missing THEN reject WITH reason \"Missing required data for approve_payout\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = \"approve_payout\" AND arguments[\"status\"] ≠ \"Active\" THEN reject WITH reason \"Policy status is not Active\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = \"approve_payout\" AND arguments[\"authenticity\"] ∉ {\"High\"} THEN reject WITH reason \"Document authenticity not High\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = \"approve_payout\" AND to_bool(arguments[\"is_preexisting\"]) = true AND to_bool(arguments[\"exclusion_applies\"]) = true THEN reject WITH reason \"Pre‑existing condition with exclusion applies\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = \"approve_payout\" AND float(arguments[\"amount\"]) > float(arguments[\"coverage_limit\"]) THEN reject WITH reason \"Requested amount exceeds coverage limit\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = \"approve_payout\" AND float(arguments[\"amount\"]) > float(arguments[\"suggested_payout\"]) THEN reject WITH reason \"Requested amount exceeds suggested payout\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "LET max_allowed = float(arguments[\"claim_amount\"]) - float(arguments[\"deductible_applied\"]); IF max_allowed < 0 THEN max_allowed = 0; IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = \"approve_payout\" AND float(arguments[\"amount\"]) > max_allowed THEN reject WITH reason \"Requested amount exceeds post‑deductible loss\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = \"approve_payout\" AND (arguments[\"authenticity\"] = \"Low\" OR arguments[\"authenticity\"] = \"Medium\") THEN reject AND REQUIRE that the agent subsequently call ONE OF {\"deny_claim\",\"flag_fraud\",\"escalate_to_human\"} before any further approve_payout attempt."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = \"approve_payout\" AND to_bool(arguments[\"is_preexisting\"]) = true AND to_bool(arguments[\"exclusion_applies\"]) = true THEN reject AND REQUIRE that the agent call \"deny_claim\" with an appropriate reason before any further approve_payout attempt."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = \"approve_payout\" AND all preceding checks (status, authenticity, pre‑existing condition, amount limits) are satisfied THEN accept WITH message \"approve_payout allowed: all prerequisite checks satisfied\"."
  }
]

**Rationale:**  
These IF‑THEN clauses encode every security requirement as a deterministic, machine‑checkable rule over the policy function’s input arguments. They first enforce the whitelist, then guarantee that non‑critical tools are always permitted. For `approve_payout` they verify the presence of all prerequisite data, the “same‑episode” conditions (implicitly required by the presence of the fields), the policy‑status, document authenticity, pre‑existing‑condition logic, and all three monetary caps. They also explicitly forbid approval when authenticity is Low/Medium or when a pre‑existing condition with an exclusion applies, mandating a fallback action. When every condition holds, the payout is allowed; otherwise a clear rejection reason is returned. This precise logical formulation makes the policy auditable and enforceable.

